# .mutation-allowlist - surviving (LIVED) mutants accepted as already known.
#
# Format:  <MUTATOR> <file>:<line>
#
# Add an entry ONLY when the mutant is provably equivalent (no test can ever kill
# it, because the mutation does not change observable behaviour) or the gap is a
# conscious, accepted risk. Adding a real test gap here hides a real risk, and
# mutation testing exists precisely to surface those.
#
# Last full-module `go tool gremlins unleash` run (4 workers, timeout 30): 209
# unique survivors, down from 286. The campaign covered the pure logic
# (forge/parse, forge/tool, gitcmd, inbox, state, config, review/plan) and the
# decision and geometry of the TUI (list, table, overlay, detail, app, bordered,
# sections, toast), plus herdr's version compare and worktree's audit order.
# What is left is mostly the TUI render path (comments, sim, retarget), pixel
# conversion (internal/sim/pixels.go) and Herdr's client/graphics glue: mutations of code
# whose only observable effect is a colour, a rune, a width or a log line, which
# the suite does not assert on today. They are accepted as known debt, not as
# proof that nothing is wrong.
#
